TITLE:: NdefRackModule
summary:: one Ndef as the rack sees it - its controls, their values, the cables into it
categories:: Libraries>NdefRack
related:: Classes/NdefRack, Classes/NdefRackSpec, Classes/NdefRackModuleView, Classes/Ndef

DESCRIPTION::
Nothing is defined twice: a module is read from its Ndef. The title is the key
and the bus, the inputs are the controls, the ranges come from
link::Classes/NdefRackSpec::, and the cables are the proxies in the node map.
You do not make these; link::Classes/NdefRack:: makes one for every Ndef it
shows.

code::
Ndef(\osc, NdefRackLib(\verbos));
m = NdefRack.at(\osc);
m.title;                          // -> "osc  ar 1"
m.paramNames;
m.param(\levels);                 // -> ( 'name': levels, 'type': array, 'size': 8, ... )
m.value(\freq);
::

A module is a dependant of its Ndef, and lets go of it when the rack drops the
module. Whatever changes the Ndef - code, the window, a patch - the module hears
of it as it happens and tells link::Classes/NdefRack::, which tells the window.

subsection:: Params

One link::Classes/Event:: per control, in the order the function declares them:
code::name::, code::rate:: (code::\control::, code::\audio::, code::\trigger::,
code::\scalar::), code::size:: (more than one for an array), code::default::,
code::spec::, code::type:: - what kind of control it is - and code::role::,
what the window draws for it (link::#*roleFor::). A library module may add
code::labels::, the names of a selector's whole-number stops
(link::Classes/NdefRackLib#*labelsFor::). Every param also has an input port in
the window.

table::
## strong::type:: || strong::for:: || strong::role, drawn as::
## code::\knob:: || a kr control || code::\bar:: - a bar with its value; code::\stepped:: when its spec steps by 1 or more, a tick per step; code::\toggle:: when that is 0 to 1, a switch
## code::\array:: || a kr control with more than one value || code::\array:: - a bar per value
## code::\audio:: || an ar control, code::\in.ar(0):: || code::\signal:: - a port only
## code::\trigger:: || a tr control, code::\t_reset:: or code::.tr:: || code::\trigger:: - a button that fires
## code::\gate:: || a kr control called code::trig::, code::gt::, code::hold:: or code::clock::, or with spec units code::"gate":: || code::\gate:: - a button that is 1 while held
::

The type comes from the name before the spec: a control called code::hold:: is
a gate whatever its range. code::type:: is what the code export, patch files,
controllers and the library's tables read; code::role:: only decides the look.

link::#-params:: keep the order the function declares;
link::#-ordered:: is the order the window draws them in, four bands
(link::#-bands::) that are the same on every module: the main inputs, timing,
the body, the tail.

code::out::, code::i_out::, code::gate:: and code::fadeTime:: are JITLib's own
and are never params.

subsection:: Voices

A library module playing several voices - see link::Classes/NdefRack#*setVoices:: -
has a value per voice in most of its controls. Such a param says
code::voice: true::, and is still drawn as one bar, button or port for every
voice; link::#-set:: sets them all. A control the library lists among the
module's code::sliders:: is drawn as a slider per voice instead (type
code::\array::).

code::
NdefRack.make(\lpf, \pad, 4);
m = NdefRack.at(\pad);
m.voices;                         // -> 4
m.title;                          // -> "pad  ×4  ar 4"
m.set(\freq, 800);                // -> [800, 800, 800, 800] in the node map
::

A mono cable into a control with a value per voice is the source once per voice
in the node map; link::#-source:: answers the source, and link::#-isSpread:: says
it is spread.

subsection:: Values

link::#-value:: is what a control's row shows: the number in the node map; on a patched
input, the number it held before the cable arrived; otherwise the function's
default. That remembered number is what link::Classes/NdefRack#*disconnect::
puts back.


CLASSMETHODS::

METHOD:: roleFor
What the window draws for a param - its type refined by its spec, the first
that fits: code::\signal:: (an audio input), code::\trigger::, code::\gate::,
code::\array::, code::\toggle:: (a code::\knob:: from 0 to 1 stepping by 1),
code::\stepped:: (a code::\knob:: stepping by 1 or more), code::\bar:: (the rest).
code::
NdefRackModule.roleFor(\knob, [0, 1, \lin, 1].asSpec);   // -> toggle
NdefRackModule.roleFor(\knob, \freq.asSpec);             // -> bar
::
ARGUMENT:: type
the param's code::type::.
ARGUMENT:: spec
its link::Classes/ControlSpec::.
RETURNS:: a link::Classes/Symbol::.

METHOD:: tailNames
The names that close a module, in this order: code::lo, hi, mix, level, amp, master::.


INSTANCEMETHODS::

METHOD:: name
The Ndef's key.

METHOD:: proxy
The link::Classes/Ndef::.

METHOD:: title
The key and the bus, code::"osc  ar 1"::; with voices, how many: code::"pad  ×4  ar 4"::.

METHOD:: voices
How many voices it plays: 1 for a mono module and for an Ndef of your own.

METHOD:: canVoice
Whether it is a library module written for voices.

METHOD:: isVoiceParam
Whether a control has a value per voice.
ARGUMENT:: key
the control.

METHOD:: typeString
code::"ar 1"::, code::"kr 8"::, or code::"empty":: for an Ndef with no bus yet.

METHOD:: rate
code::\audio::, code::\control::, or nil before the Ndef has a bus.

METHOD:: numChannels
How many channels its output carries.

METHOD:: isAudio
METHOD:: isControl
Its rate.

METHOD:: isEmpty
Whether the Ndef has nothing playing into its bus - an Ndef patched from before
it was ever defined.

METHOD:: isMonitoring
Whether it is playing to the outputs.

METHOD:: canBus
Whether it is a bus module, reading one of BusManager's buses by name or a bus index - or writing to it.

METHOD:: writesBus
Whether it is a bus module that writes to its bus: code::send::, code::throw::,
code::sendpan::, code::replace::, code::blend::, code::insert:: - an
code::insert:: on a control bus only reads it.

METHOD:: busVerb
What it does with its bus, for a sentence - "reads" for an code::insert:: on a control bus.
RETURNS:: a link::Classes/String:: - code::"reads"::, code::"writes to":: or code::"reads and writes"::.

METHOD:: bus
What it reads or writes to: the name of a BusManager bus, a bus index of your own, or nil - what
link::Classes/NdefRack#*setBus:: takes.

METHOD:: busInfo
What it reads or writes to, from its source: code::(name:, index:, channels:, rate:):: - name nil
for a bus index of your own; see link::Classes/NdefRackLib#*busFor:: - or nil for a
module that is not a bus module.

METHOD:: canSpeakers
Whether it is a library module panning among the speakers of a setup.

METHOD:: speakers
The name of its speaker setup - what link::Classes/NdefRack#*setSpeakers:: takes - or nil.

METHOD:: speakerInfo
code::(name:, setup:)::, from its source - see
link::Classes/NdefRackLib#*speakersFor:: - or nil.

METHOD:: speakersKnown
Whether link::Classes/NdefRackSpeakers:: has that name, and these speakers under it.

METHOD:: kind
The library module it was made from, or nil for an Ndef of your own.

METHOD:: params
Every param, see link::#Params::.

METHOD:: param
One param by name, or nil.

METHOD:: paramNames
Every param's name.

METHOD:: ordered
Every param, in the order the window draws them and a controller's page
(link::Classes/NdefRackKtl#*follow::) runs: link::#-bands:: one after the other.
Worked out on each call; nothing is kept.
RETURNS:: an link::Classes/Array:: of Events.

METHOD:: bands
The params in four bands, each in the order the function declares them unless
said otherwise:
table::
## strong::1. main inputs:: || code::in::, code::in1:: ..., code::a::, code::b::, any rate; the first audio one sits on the main row, level with the output
## strong::2. timing:: || the gates, then code::rate:: when the module has a gate or a trigger, then the triggers
## strong::3. body:: || everything else
## strong::4. tail:: || link::#*tailNames::, in that order
::
RETURNS:: an link::Classes/Array:: of four Arrays of Events.

METHOD:: outs
The names of the output's channels, from the library module's code::outs:: -
only when there are exactly as many names as channels.
RETURNS:: an link::Classes/Array:: of link::Classes/String::s, or nil.

METHOD:: value
What the row for that control shows.

METHOD:: source
The proxy a cable brings into that control - also when it comes in once per
voice - or nil.

METHOD:: isPatched
Whether a cable is plugged into that control.

METHOD:: isSpread
Whether the cable into that control is a mono source spread over every voice.

METHOD:: cableFor
What the node map holds for a cable into a control: the source proxy, or - a
mono source into a control with a value per voice - the proxy once per voice.
ARGUMENT:: key
the control.
ARGUMENT:: src
the source link::Classes/NodeProxy::.

METHOD:: fit
A value made as wide as the voices, for a control with a value per voice: one
number on every voice; an array cut, or lengthened with its last value. Any other
value, and any other control, as it is.
ARGUMENT:: key
the control.
ARGUMENT:: value
a number or an array.

METHOD:: inputs
Every cable into this module, code::[paramName, sourceProxy]:: for each.

METHOD:: reads
The proxies its source function reads by itself, with code::Ndef.ar(\x)::.

METHOD:: settings
The numbers and arrays in its node map, as key value pairs - what the code
export writes for it.

METHOD:: copyValues
What a copy of this module starts from, as key value pairs: every control's value -
a patched one, the value it had before its cable - except where it is the default
anyway, and never a trigger, which would fire on arrival.

METHOD:: display
The display its library entry asks for - code::\scope::, code::\spectrum:: - or
nil.

METHOD:: set
code::Ndef(name).set(key, value):: - on every voice, for a control with a value
per voice (see link::#-fit::).

METHOD:: reset
The function's default back on a control, and the node map left as if the control
had never moved. A patched input is left alone; unplug it first.

METHOD:: lastValues
The last number each control held, key -> value.

METHOD:: release
Stop hearing from the Ndef. The rack calls this when it drops the module.
